! Silicon, eight atoms in the conventional cubic cell, at 20 Ry, on a 3x3x3 mesh
! with symmetry off: 27 k-points.
!
! The one benchmark here that is not single k-point, on purpose: it is where the
! batching over k shows, which is what memory mode's one k-point a call, a k-chunk
! sized to the card (k_batch = 'fit') and speed mode's whole-axis batch differ in
! (PERFORMANCE.md, "Memory mode on a k-mesh" and "A k-chunk sized to the card").
! Against pw.x a multi-k timing measures batching rather than the physics, so it is
! not one of the compare_qe.py inputs.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=1, celldm(1) =10.20,
    nat=8, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=20.0, nosym=.true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.00 0.50 0.50
 Si 0.50 0.00 0.50
 Si 0.50 0.50 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
 Si 0.25 0.75 0.75
 Si 0.75 0.25 0.75
 Si 0.75 0.75 0.25
K_POINTS automatic
 3 3 3 0 0 0
